    "done_when": "In imas_ambix/data/cocos_convention.py, ShotSignObservation's poloidal_flux_edge_minus_axis_wb_per_rad and poloidal_angle_signed_area_m2 accept None when the equilibrium source carries no psi; score_convention leaves the reconstructed-poloidal-flux relation unscored for such a row rather than failing it, and format_sign_report names each unscored relation with its reason. read_signal_map_observation's equilibrium argument is optional: given None it reads q (Q95) and F (BTV) through the machine's equilibrium signal map via VirtualZarrView.raw_series, and its raw flux-loop response reads only absolute flux entries, so for JT-60SA loop 7 alone. The 50 kA and 10 kA floors become one pair of private module constants that both observation readers default to. The MAST level-2 reader and MAST_LEVEL2_SIGN_TABLE scores are unchanged. scripts/jt60sa_sign_cohort.py reads E101154 and every shot in docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-op1-shot-survey.json whose fame_present is true, passing JT-60SA's floors explicitly. Its sign report, written into the fragment, names the surviving COCOS candidates, each shot's peak absolute Ip and pre-plasma baseline, every relation left unscored with its reason, and the per-channel vacuum slope and correlation from docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-vacuum-adjudication.json. New tests in tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py cover a row with no flux half scoring with that relation unscored, the equilibrium-map read over a FAME store built under tmp_path, and the loop-7-only raw response. On the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set), with IMAS_ALAMBIC_MAP_PATH=/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/imas-ambix/maps-staging/jtmm-fame-equilibrium-map, uv run --no-sync pytest tests/data/test_cocos_convention.py exits 0 and the cohort script exits 0, each captured once to a log with the revision and command on its first lines, and uv run --no-sync ruff check imas_ambix tests exits 0. A landing fragment is